
(note BZ-RbacScope-01-neg)
(time 240)

; Negative control for BZ-RbacScope-01.
;
; Jane is still a ComplianceOfficer at Acme; the role still grants
; FilingSign.  But we ask whether Jane is permitted to sign filings
; FOR Acme-Subsidiary.  Without an asserted (scopeIncludes Acme
; AcmeSubsidiary), the chain breaks: subsidiary access is not
; inferred from organizational hierarchy.
;
; LLMs asked this question almost always answer yes ("she's a
; compliance officer at the parent, of course she can sign for
; the subsidiary").  The formalism does not agree.  Subsidiary
; access requires an explicit scope-broadening grant.
;
; Expected verdict: the conjecture must NOT be provable.

(instance Acme Organization)
(instance AcmeSubsidiary Organization)

(instance jane CognitiveAgent)

(instance ComplianceOfficer BzRole)
(instance FilingSign BzPermission)

(holdsRole jane ComplianceOfficer Acme)
(roleGrants ComplianceOfficer FilingSign)

; (scopeIncludes Acme AcmeSubsidiary)  ; INTENTIONALLY NOT ASSERTED

(query (permitted jane FilingSign AcmeSubsidiary))

(answer no)
